## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Spoken Places
## Notes: Zone and subzone lore on the world map, read aloud through Spoken.
## Notes-deDE: Zonen- und Gebietslore auf der Weltkarte, vorgelesen durch Spoken.
## Notes-esES: Historia de zonas y subzonas en el mapa del mundo, leída en voz alta a través de Spoken.
## Notes-esMX: Historia de zonas y subzonas en el mapa del mundo, leída en voz alta a través de Spoken.
## Notes-frFR: Histoire des zones et sous-zones sur la carte du monde, lue à voix haute grâce à Spoken.
## Notes-ptBR: História de zonas e subzonas no mapa do mundo, lida em voz alta através do Spoken.
## Notes-ruRU: История зон и подзон на карте мира, озвученная через Spoken.
## Notes-koKR: Spoken으로 월드맵의 지역과 하위 지역 전승을 소리내어 읽습니다.
## Notes-zhCN: 在世界地图上通过 Spoken 朗读区域和次级区域传说。
## Notes-zhTW: 在世界地圖上透過 Spoken 朗讀區域和次級區域傳說。
## Version: 3.5.1
## Author: rusty
## SavedVariables: SpokenZonesSettings
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: SpokenZonesCharacter
## LoadSavedVariablesFirst: true
# ^ load-bearing beyond convenience: the generated data files under Data/ ask
# Language.lua which language to build a table for, and it can only answer that
# early because SpokenZonesSettings is already populated. Without this line every player
# silently reads English.
## Dependencies: Spoken
# Spoken is what this module runs on, and ships in the same zip.
## OptionalDeps: SpokenZonesAudio, ZoneLoreAudio, ZoneLoreAudio64
# The packs are not a registration mechanism: they register themselves into
# SpokenZonesAudioPacks and Audio.lua walks that on demand, so this list is load order only.
#
# Both pack folder names are listed: SpokenZonesAudio is what ships now, ZoneLoreAudio
# what a player installed before the rename, and ZoneLoreAudio64 the retired smaller
# tier. A name here that nobody has installed costs nothing.
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\Spoken_Places\Textures\AddonIcon.tga
## Group: Spoken
## X-License: Addon code MIT. Zone lore text from warcraft.wiki.gg, CC BY-SA 4.0.
## X-Credits: Lore text sourced from warcraft.wiki.gg contributors (CC BY-SA 4.0).


# Data/Languages.lua first: it is what Language.lua reads to decide which
# language is being read, and everything after that guards itself on the answer.
